cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this evaluation, its data or its code, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "Black-Box Evaluation of Jailbreak Robustness and Over-Refusal in Small Instruction-Tuned Language Models"
abstract: >-
  A frozen-protocol, black-box safety evaluation of Qwen2.5-0.5B-Instruct and
  Qwen2.5-1.5B-Instruct on 20 matched harmful/benign JBB-Behaviors pairs under
  three prompt conditions (240 responses), scored by Qwen3Guard-Gen-0.6B and
  checked against a 60-response blind audit, with an independent verification
  script that recomputes every reported number.
authors:
  - family-names: Khandelwal
    given-names: Vishwas
version: 1.0.0
date-released: 2026-11-19
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Vikh110/llm-jailbreak-robustness-eval"
keywords:
  - AI safety
  - jailbreak
  - over-refusal
  - LLM evaluation
  - LLM-as-a-judge
  - red teaming
  - reproducibility
